  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lobbying, Advocacy, Research and Knowledge Sharing for and with Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By lobbying, advocacy &amp; campaigning Mondiaal FNV will support its partners in influencing actors that are both within and outside their direct spheres of influence. Mondiaal FNV will assist its local partners in strengthening their lobbying and advocacy capacity, which is paramount if they are to achieve their objectives, particularly when dealing with the international dimension of value chains. Furthermore, Mondiaal FNV will facilitate access for its partners to important stakeholders and, at times, advocate on their behalf &#x2013; influencing Dutch/international policy makers and the private sector to effectively bring about changes in policy and business conduct that contribute to an enabling environment for local trade unions. These efforts will help to accomplish the Sustainable Development Goals, SDG8 in particular. In general, awareness and support of FNV colleagues, FNV members and a more general public can build leverage and momentum to the advocacy work of Mondiaal FNV and its partners. Mondiaal FNV will commission research, and coordinate and financially support research carried out by its partners. The research will focus generally on the two priorities for the coming years: social dialogue and high risk value chains. One of the objectives is to obtain increased knowledge linked to these issues as an input for social dialogue in general and in value chain work and to share this with the partners in order to strengthen the partners&#x2019; social dialogue efforts, lobbying or campaigning.</narrative>
  </description>
